n issues, or D (concentrates well). We need to decide if we shift vote.\n\nWe have evidence: B weak memory for numbers (attention/accuracy concern). C has excellent attention skills (strength). C also makes correct decisions quickly, calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, puts concern for others above everything. But C has difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Those are concerns for crew cooperation and adaptability.\n\nD has concentration, problem solving, responsibility, but moody, loner, hot temper. No explicit memory issues.\n\nA has anticipation, leadership, but unfriendly, not open to new ideas, show-off.\n\nGiven B's memory weakness, maybe we should reconsider. Which candidate has best overall? C has excellent attention, good decision making, calm, but communication issues. D has strong problem solving and responsibility, but temperament issues. B has reliability and stress handling but memory weakness.\n\nWe need to decide if B still best. The memory weakness could affect safety-critical tasks (e.g., fuel calculations). That is serious. Perhaps we should shift to Candidate C, whose attention is excellent, decision quality high, calmness, and concern for others (crew cooperation). Communication difficulty is a concern but maybe less severe than memory weakness? Egocentric and unwilling to further education also concerns.\n\nAlternatively D has strong concentration and responsibility, but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to weigh. The panel hasn't discussed attention and accuracy for other candidates. We could ask about C's attention? We have note: C has excellent attention skills. So that's a strength. Also C puts concern for others above everything, which helps crew cooperation. However egocentric may counter that. But \"puts concern for others above everything\" suggests good teamwork. Egocentric contradictory. Might need clarification.\n\nGiven the new evidence, I think we should a